  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a comprehensive database system named `MovieBank`, aimed at cataloging movies with detailed information about associated actors, directors, and genres. This system is designed to organize and manage movie-related data efficiently, facilitating easy access and management.\n\nObjectives\n\n- Create a structured database to store detailed information on movies, actors, directors, and genres.\n- Enable tracking of movie ratings and associations between movies and actors.\n- Facilitate retrieval and updating of data concerning movies and their attributes.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Database Administrators: Responsible for maintaining and managing the database.\n- Content Managers: Use the database to input and update movie-related data.\n- Developers: Integrate the database with other applications or interfaces.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Movie Information Management:\n   - Store details of movies including title, release date, duration, genre, director, and description.\n   - Link each movie to specific genre(s) and director(s).\n\n2. Actor and Director Details:\n   - Catalog information on actors and directors, including name, birth date, nationality, website, and biography.\n   - Capture relationships where actors may also serve as directors.\n\n3. Genre Cataloging:\n   - Maintain a list of genres with a unique ID, name, and description.\n\n4. Rating System:\n   - Track ratings associated with individual movies through a dedicated ratings table.\n\n5. Associative Entities:\n   - Record the connections between movies and actors using an associative table to manage many-to-many relationships.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Data Integrity: Ensure referential integrity using foreign keys across tables.\n- Scalability: The database should efficiently handle an expanding volume of entries as more movies, actors, and directors are cataloged.\n- Performance: Optimize queries to ensure quick retrieval and update of data.\n- Security: Implement measures to safeguard data against unauthorized access or breaches.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0205\nCREATE TABLE `genres` (\n  `genre_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`genre_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `name` (`name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `directors` (\n  `director_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `birth_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `website` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`director_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `actors` (\n  `actor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `birth_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `website` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`actor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `movies` (\n  `movie_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `duration_minutes` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `genre_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `director_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`movie_id`),\n  KEY `genre_id` (`genre_id`),\n  KEY `director_id` (`director_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `movies_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`genre_id`) REFERENCES `genres` (`genre_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `movies_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`director_id`) REFERENCES `directors` (`director_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `movie_actors` (\n  `movie_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `actor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `character_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`movie_id`,`actor_id`),\n  KEY `actor_id` (`actor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `movie_actors_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`movie_id`) REFERENCES `movies` (`movie_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `movie_actors_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`actor_id`) REFERENCES `actors` (`actor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ratings` (\n  `rating_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `movie_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating_value` decimal(3,1) NOT NULL,\n  `rating_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `source` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rating_id`),\n  KEY `movie_id` (`movie_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ratings_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`movie_id`) REFERENCES `movies` (`movie_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
